// Matrix calls bench_matrix.
//
// Makes one workbench a cell of the grid, alike a laboratory workbench - its days, markets, account and costs - on every combination of the tick models, spread multipliers, slippages (as bench_create_alike takes them), latencies, commissions (as bench_create takes one), execution models (partial fills, a touched limit's and a rejection's chance) and seeds given: what a robustness check runs one policy over. A seed seeds a cell's seeded path, its random slippage and its execution model's draws; a combination with none of them draws nothing, so it is made once, at the first seed, and the answer says how many were collapsed. Before it answers, the matrix is written to the trial ledger as one trial of as many candidates as it has cells (family bench_matrix unless named), so a result read off any cell is counted with everything else tried; a cell's result is ledger_record's kind result, of that trial. At most 256 cells; a tick model the recording cannot make is refused and no cell is kept. Each cell's workbench is marked with the grid it is of (the workbench it was made alike and the trial). Answers each cell's workbench and conditions, and the trial's sequence number; with dry_run, what it would make and nothing made.
// Scope: lab. Since: 4.0.0.
//   - bench: The laboratory workbench every cell is made alike.
//   - dry_run: Answer what the grid would make - its cells' conditions, how many, how many were collapsed, a refusal of its size, and the tick models the recording can make - and make nothing, write nothing.
