// BarsWindow calls bars_window.
//
// Answers the closed bars of several of a workbench's markets (1-64) in several frames (1-16: intervals, or a chart's elements as {chart}) cut at ONE instant: the cursor, or aligned_to an interval's last close, so every frame ends where that bar ended. A bar is a row when it closed at or before the cut; the newest limit rows per frame (200 when omitted, at most 5000; symbols x frames x limit at most 200000), oldest first, in columns time_ms, open, high, low, close, tick_volume, spread_points; nothing past the cursor. include_forming hands an interval's forming bar beside its rows. A frame not ready refuses the call by name unless partial, which answers what is ready and lists not_ready. zone cuts every interval frame in a time zone of the caller's choosing (a day at its midnight, H4 on its grid), folded from the workbench's finer candles, the screen untouched; time_ms stays the workbench's own stamps. The input a forecasting model reads.
// Scope: read. Since: 3.3.0.
//   - bench: The workbench's uri, as `get_state` gives it.
//   - frames: The frames, 1 to 16: intervals' labels, or {"chart": uri} for a chart's elements.
//   - aligned_to: Where every frame is cut: "cursor" (the default), or an interval's label — that interval's last close.
//   - include_forming: true hands each interval's bar still forming beside its rows, marked forming; it is never a row.
//   - limit: Closed bars per frame per market, newest kept: 200 when omitted, at most 5000. symbols × frames × limit is at most 200000.
//   - partial: true answers what is ready and lists the rest in not_ready; omitted or false, a frame not ready refuses the call.
//   - symbol: One market, in place of symbols.
//   - symbols: The markets, 1 to 64, each one of the workbench's.
//   - zone: The time zone every interval frame is cut in, aligned_to read in too: a code from zones_list, an IANA name, system, or display (the workbench's charts' zone). Omitted, the workbench's own cut, as its venue reads it.
func (a *DataAPI) BarsWindow(ctx context.Context, args DataBarsWindowArgs) (any, error) {
	return a.c.Call(ctx, "bars_window", args)
}

