// RunRobustness calls run_robustness.
//
// Tests how robust an ended run of this session is, over its trades read with their entries, every draw from one fixed seed: the maximum drawdown over the trades drawn again in another order, the net with a tenth of the trades left out, the net with each trade's fill degraded by up to a tenth of the median absolute trade net (each as 5th, 50th and 95th percentiles of 1,000 draws); the random-entry percentile (the share of random draws - as many trades, each held as long as one of the run's, at a random minute in a random direction on its first market - whose sum of price moves is below the run's); and its trades, net and wins under the quiet, middle and busy days; and its metrics - Van Tharp's SQN, expectancy and its parts, the longest drawdown duration and the market's own trading days a year. Each with its definition; kept as robustness.json beside the run's run.json. The Run window's Validation tab draws the same.
// Scope: read. Since: 1.14.0.
