// StatsFamilyTest calls stats_family_test.
//
// Tests a family of candidates against a benchmark at once, from each candidate's performance less the benchmark's period by period: Hansen's test for superior predictive ability (the consistent p-value, with the liberal one and the conservative one, which is White's reality check) and each candidate's Romano-Wolf stepdown adjusted p-value, over one stationary bootstrap drawn the same for every candidate. The same series and seed give the same answer. Pure arithmetic: reads and writes nothing; a family larger than candidates x periods x resamples = 200,000,000 is refused with its size.
// Scope: read. Since: 1.17.0.
//   - series: Each candidate's performance less the benchmark's, period by period (larger is better), every row the same length: one row a candidate.
//   - mean_block: The stationary bootstrap's mean block length in periods; omitted, 10.
//   - resamples: Bootstrap resamples; omitted, 1,000; at most 20,000.
//   - seed: The bootstrap's seed (the same seed, the same answer); omitted, 1.
func (a *StrategyAPI) StatsFamilyTest(ctx context.Context, args StrategyStatsFamilyTestArgs) (any, error) {
	return a.c.Call(ctx, "stats_family_test", args)
}

